= Land Reform

Agriculture remains one of the most pressing issues facing the republic, particularly due to the overwhelming control exerted by large landowners over Turkish agriculture. This concentration of land ownership severely hinders rural development and contributes to significant migration from the countryside to urban centers. Addressing the question of land ownership is therefore essential.

Since the foundation of the republic, our party has consistently regarded land reform and equitable distribution as necessary prerequisites for rural development. Although Atatürk did not live long enough to implement what may have been one of his most influential reforms, it is now the responsibility of the current generation to realize this vision.

However, it is first necessary to determine a unified policy platform from among the proposals currently circulating within the party.

Current status: [? if land_reform == 0 : No concrete land reform policy has been adopted. ?][? if land_reform == 1 : We have committed to establishing rural cooperatives. ?][? if land_reform == 2 : We have promised comprehensive land distribution programs. ?][? if land_reform == 3 : We have announced the ambitious Köykent village-city project. ?]

- @koykent: Propose the Köykent project - transforming rural areas through planned village-cities.
- @land_distribution: Commit to redistributing large estates to small farmers.
- @cooperatives: Establish agricultural cooperatives to support small farmers.
- @root: We cannot take action on land reform right now.
- @easy_discard

@koykent
view-if: land_reform < 3
subtitle: Radical reform
on-arrival: {! AnatolianCardActions.commitAdvisor(Q); !} land_reform = 3; left_kemalists_dissent -= 5; kemalist_marxists_dissent -= 5

The Köykent project, proposed by Ecevit, constitutes a comprehensive reform intended to reorganize rural areas and dispersed villages into larger, city-like entities specializing in agriculture. Both the Leftist Kemalist and Marxist Kemalist factions have expressed support for this initiative.

The party leadership has announced its intention to include the Köykent project in its policy platform. However, persuading the remainder of the party to our plans is expected to require significant effort and time.

@land_distribution
view-if: land_reform < 2
subtitle: Significant reform
on-arrival: {! AnatolianCardActions.commitAdvisor(Q); !} land_reform = 2; left_kemalists_dissent -= 3;

The party has committed to an extensive land distribution program, pledging to break up large estates and allocate land to small-scale farmers. This initiative has received public endorsement from both the Leftist Kemalist and Reformist Kemalist factions.

The party leadership has stated that land distribution will be prioritized within the policy platform. However, achieving broader party consensus is anticipated to require significant effort and time.

@cooperatives
view-if: land_reform < 1
subtitle: Modest reform
on-arrival: {! AnatolianCardActions.commitAdvisor(Q); !} land_reform = 1; orthodox_kemalists_dissent -= 5

We have announced support for the establishment of agricultural cooperatives to enable small farmers to access credit, equipment, and markets. Although the scale is modest, this cooperative strategy reflects our ongoing commitment to rural development. Both Reformist Kemalist and Right Kemalist factions have expressed their support.

The party leadership has announced its intention to include rural cooperatives in the policy platform. However, persuading the remainder of the party, particularly those on the Left due to how minimal it is, will require sustained effort and time.

@root

We cannot pursue land reform initiatives at this time.
